<BaseLayout title="Data licence" description="Licence, attribution and third-party rights for APT Notes public data and static APIs.">
  <article class="shell narrow prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Reuse boundary</p>
    <h1>Data licence</h1>
    <p class="lead">APT Notes makes its original structured research reusable while preserving the rights and attribution attached to underlying sources.</p>

    <h2 id="original-data">HECAVEX original data</h2>
    <p>HECAVEX-authored summaries, classifications and original structured fields in the public APT Notes JSON exports are licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)</a>, unless a record states otherwise.</p>
    <p>When reusing that material, credit “HECAVEX APT Notes”, link to <a href="https://apt.hecavex.com/">apt.hecavex.com</a>, identify material changes, and retain the record's review date, confidence and source references.</p>

    <h2 id="third-party-material">Third-party material</h2>
    <p>The CC BY 4.0 grant does not relicense source publications, quoted material, vendor or government assessments, MITRE ATT&amp;CK content, logos, trademarks, or material reached through external links. Those items remain subject to their owners' terms. A source citation records provenance; it is not a redistribution grant.</p>

    <h2 id="software-and-brand">Software and brand</h2>
    <p>This data licence does not grant rights to HECAVEX names, marks or visual identity. The original software used to operate apt.hecavex.com is covered by the repository's <a href="https://github.com/Hecavex/apt.hecavex.com/blob/main/LICENSE">MIT licence</a>; that licence does not relicense research or brand material. The deployed local-search runtime retains its <a href="/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt">Pagefind and vscode-ripgrep notices</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="no-endorsement">No endorsement or warranty</h2>
    <p>Attribution does not imply HECAVEX endorses a derivative work. The data is provided as best-effort public research without warranties, continuous monitoring or an operational-response SLA. Read the <a href="/about/methodology/">methodology and limitations</a> before using it.</p>

    <h2>Questions and corrections</h2>
    <p>For a licensing question or correction, use the <a href="https://hecavex.com/en/contact/">HECAVEX contact channel</a>. Report accidental sensitive-data publication through the <a href="/security/">security policy</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
